shape theory.coherence.contact-is-shape : theory.contact, theory.shape, theory.coherence.law0 {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 5.7 (Contact Is a Shape).
// Contact between shapes is itself a shape. It persists (the
// relationship endures across moments), has internal structure
// (the geometry of the contact), and has character (the reference
// content carried across the boundary). As a shape, the contact
// shape is in self-contact and must satisfy the Laws of Coherence.
//
// This is the recursion of the theory. Contact is a shape. The
// contact shape is in self-contact. The self-contact of the contact
// shape is itself a shape. The recursion grounds at the axiom:
// persistence is the capacity to change while maintaining continuity.
// At every level, the same laws apply because at every level, the
// same axiom holds. This is not infinite regress; it is fractal
// coherence.
//
// Derives from: theory.contact (contact persists and has structure),
//               theory.shape (anything that persists is a shape),
//               theory.coherence.law0 (shapes must cohere)
  """
}
